WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.270
Before we say goodbye, let's play a quick round of-

2
00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:07.270
Drewth or dare.
(audience cheers and claps)

3
00:00:07.955 --> 00:00:09.872
All right, we have Malik.

4
00:00:09.872 --> 00:00:11.610 line:15%
Hi Malik.
Hi!

5
00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.660 line:15%
All right, truth or dare?

6
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.600 line:15%
Truth or dare, what is the most random thing we might find

7
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.900 line:15%
in either of your closets?

8
00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:22.350
I bought a pair of boots once.

9
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.607
It was after a happy hour where it was like,

10
00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:25.640
"Oh yeah, these are cute."

11
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.637
And then like the next morning, I was like,

12
00:00:26.637 --> 00:00:27.527
"Those aren't cute.

13
00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.360
"Those are cute."

14
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.230
But you kept 'em.

15
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.078
I kept 'em because maybe there'll be cute one day.

16
00:00:32.078 --> 00:00:33.900
They're like a Doc Martin, but like a platform.

17
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.130
What am I doing?

18
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.457
Like I'm going to a rave.
That is so not you.

19
00:00:36.457 --> 00:00:39.690
No, no.
I have this really bizarre,

20
00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.670
it's my favorite store in New York City.

21
00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:45.140
If you're ever in town, please go to Abracadabra.

22
00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.020
They have vintage stuff.

23
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.650
It's like a dream, everything you could ever imagine.

24
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:54.060
And I got this crazy head dress with horns and feathers

25
00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.600
and pearls that go.

26
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.840
And I just keep it in there because every once in a while,

27
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.040
it's just time to put that thing on.

28
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.570
Yes, and do a walk around the house.

29
00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.927
And you would see it in the closet and you're like,

30
00:01:04.927 --> 00:01:07.077
"Oh okay, that's an outlier."

31
00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.823
And yet I love supporting it whenever I can.

32
00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:12.693
What about you?

33
00:01:12.693 --> 00:01:14.000
Anything rando in your closet?

34
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.950
I have a leather black and white cowboy jacket

35
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.986
with tassels all up and down the back.

36
00:01:18.986 --> 00:01:20.510
Yeah!
Oh my God.

37
00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:22.890
Hey, I'll trade you a pair of boots for that jacket.

38
00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:23.723
I want that.

39
00:01:23.723 --> 00:01:25.520
Or maybe you need to put your boots

40
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.030
and the jacket together.

41
00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:27.870
With your head dress.

42
00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:28.703
We got a look.

43
00:01:28.703 --> 00:01:31.866
Well Malik, I would love to see you in that jacket.

44
00:01:31.866 --> 00:01:33.090
Thank you everybody

45
00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.730
for choosing to spend your time here with us.

46
00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.543
We make this show for you.
(audience clap)

47
00:01:38.543 --> 00:01:41.788
So, take it with you!
Take it with you!

48
00:01:41.788 --> 00:01:44.371 line:15%
(upbeat music)

